<article class="env-corollary" id="04CR">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04CR">Corollary <span data-tag="04CR">8.6.2.4</span>.</a> Every cocartesian fibration of simplicial sets $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits a cartesian conjugate. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Corollary <a data-tag="029F" href="/tag/029F">5.6.7.3</a>, we can choose a pullback diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{U} \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' \ar [d]^{U'} \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}', } \]
</div>
<p>
       where $U'$ is a cocartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories. By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="04CA" href="/tag/04CA">8.6.1.4</a>, it will suffice to show that $U'$ admits a cartesian conjugate, which follows from Proposition <a data-tag="04CQ" href="/tag/04CQ">8.6.2.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
